@prefix tmk:     <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/> .
@prefix tmkc:    <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix time:    <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/time>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "TM-Knowledge — time module"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """Dates, currency, versions, and what this corpus cannot answer about time.

**The versioning model is defined here (the second review response, A03; S045).**
An instrument and a provision are enduring: `tmk:doc/TMA1995` is the Act whatever
its text, `TMA1995/s44` is section 44 whatever its words, and the instrument carries
the Federal Register's own enduring id (`tmk:registerTitleId`, `C2004A04969`). A
`tmk:Compilation` is one versioned text of an instrument, with its own register id,
in force over a `time:Interval` that begins on its start date and whose end is not
stated until a later compilation is held: an interval with no `time:hasEnd` has an
end not known, never 'no end'. Legal effect and capture are kept apart: the interval
is when the text was law; `tmk:capturedAt` and `tmk:currentAtCapture` are when
upstream read it and what the Register then said of it. A provision's text and hash
in the source graph are its text in one compilation (`tmk:textFrom`).

**Selection waits for a second version.** The snapshot holds one compilation per
instrument, so 'which text applied on «date»' has four honest answers today
(`tmk:VersionState`): held, not held (before the held start), after the capture
(a later one may have started) and no date given. `tm_knowledge.versions` computes
them; it never decides which date governs a question. Holding a second compilation
means capturing it upstream (CLAUDE.md rule 2).

The Manual is different and unchanged: there is no corpus-level version stamp for it
(Q-05); its amendment history is the upstream repository's git history, and 'what
guidance was current on «date»' needs a full-history clone, a different data
strategy rather than a different query. CQ-0014 stays out of scope on that line.

What the module also carries is the currency mechanism that works for both: staleness
by content hash. An assertion whose source hash no longer matches the pin is stale
and returns to review. That is Stage 10's whole incremental mechanism and it needs no
version stamp."""@en-AU ;
    owl:imports <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ns/provenance> ;
    owl:versionInfo "draft — not approved" .

tmk:AuthorityStatus a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Authority status"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether an authority is current, superseded or repealed."@en-AU .

tmk:Current a tmk:AuthorityStatus ; rdfs:label "current"@en-AU .

tmk:Superseded a tmk:AuthorityStatus ; rdfs:label "superseded"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "'Every superseded instruction has a status date' — one of the six starting SHACL rules."@en-AU .

tmk:NotHeld a tmk:AuthorityStatus ; rdfs:label "not held"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """Cited by the corpus and held nowhere in the programme.

Not a defect and not a gap to be filled by guessing: s 114 of the *Trade Marks
Act 1905* is cited by Part 29.3.1, the instrument is not in this corpus, and it
can be neither excluded (the Manual relies on it) nor resolved (Q-24). 17
distinct refs cited from the in-scope chunks are in this state, and CQ-0020 asks
for exactly this list."""@en-AU .

tmk:authorityStatus a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:range tmk:AuthorityStatus ;
    rdfs:label "authority status"@en-AU .

tmk:statusDate a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "status date"@en-AU .

tmk:capturedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "captured at"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "When upstream captured the passage. The nearest thing this corpus has to a currency date, and it is a capture time, not an in-force date."@en-AU .

tmk:compilationNumber a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "compilation number"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Which compilation of the instrument the pinned snapshot holds, numbered as the Federal Register of Legislation numbers it. Read from upstream's `instrument.json`. No domain since S045: a `tmk:Compilation` carries it too, and the instrument's value is its held compilation's."@en-AU .

tmk:registerId a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "register id"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The Federal Register of Legislation's id for that compilation (`C2024C00545`): the one name a reader can look up. No domain since S045: a `tmk:Compilation` carries it too."@en-AU .

tmk:compilationStart a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Legislation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:label "in force from"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The date the held compilation is in force from. Every answer names it ('the Act as in force from 14 October 2024'), because the law moves and the snapshot does not until the pin does."@en-AU .

tmk:lastAmended a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Page ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "last amended"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual page's own amendment note where it carries one. Page-level and self-reported — not a version stamp, and not comparable across pages."@en-AU .

tmk:isStale a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "is stale"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The `tmk:sourceContentHash` on an assertion or an evidence anchor no longer matches the pinned snapshot: the passage under it moved. Computed at build time, never asserted by hand. No domain since S041, because anchors carry it too."@en-AU .


# --- the versioning model (A03, S045) ----------------------------------------
# OWL-Time supplies the interval and its instants; nothing here re-declares them.

tmk:Compilation a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Compilation"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment """One versioned text of an instrument, as the Federal Register numbers and identifies it (compilation 48 of the Act, `C2026C00421`). Distinct from `tmk:DocumentVersion`, which is a capture of the corpus (the pin): a compilation is a state of the law, a capture is when it was read. Minted as `tmk:doc/TMA1995/compilation/48`."""@en-AU .

tmk:compilationOf a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Compilation ;
    rdfs:range tmk:Legislation ;
    rdfs:label "compilation of"@en-AU .

tmk:heldCompilation a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Legislation ;
    rdfs:range tmk:Compilation ;
    rdfs:label "held compilation"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "A compilation of this instrument the pinned snapshot holds. Not functional: one today, several once upstream captures history. The instrument-level `tmk:compilationNumber`, `tmk:registerId` and `tmk:compilationStart` describe the one held, and stay for the readers that use them."@en-AU .

tmk:registerTitleId a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Legislation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "register title id"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The Federal Register's id for the instrument itself (`C2004A04969` for the Act), which every compilation shares: the enduring identity, where `tmk:registerId` names one text."@en-AU .

tmk:inForceDuring a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Compilation ;
    rdfs:range time:Interval ;
    rdfs:label "in force during"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "When the compilation's text was the law: a `time:Interval` whose `time:hasBeginning` is its start date. Its `time:hasEnd` is stated only when the next compilation is held; absent, the end is not known."@en-AU .

tmk:currentAtCapture a owl:DatatypeProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:domain tmk:Compilation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "current at capture"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the Register showed this compilation as in force, with no amendment left unincorporated, on the day upstream captured it (`tmk:capturedAt`). The only evidence that the interval reached the capture date. Absent where upstream did not say."@en-AU .

tmk:textFrom a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:range tmk:Compilation ;
    rdfs:label "text from"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The compilation a provision's or unit's text and `tmk:contentHash` are taken from. The provision is enduring; its words are this compilation's. An evidence anchor on it was read against this text when it is not stale. No domain: provisions and units both carry it."@en-AU .

tmk:VersionState a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Version state"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "What can be said of the text of an instrument in force on a date, given what is held (`tm_knowledge.versions.STATES`). Never inferred from silence: each is computed from the held compilations and a date the caller names."@en-AU .

tmk:VersionHeld a tmk:VersionState ; rdfs:label "held"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The date falls in a held compilation's interval; for the latest, on or before its capture and only where it was current at capture."@en-AU .

tmk:VersionNotHeld a tmk:VersionState ; rdfs:label "not held"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The date is before the earliest held compilation began: the text then in force is one the snapshot does not hold."@en-AU .

tmk:VersionAfterCapture a tmk:VersionState ; rdfs:label "after capture"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The date is after the latest held compilation was captured: a later compilation may have started, and the held text is not assumed to apply."@en-AU .

tmk:VersionUnconfirmed a tmk:VersionState ; rdfs:label "unconfirmed"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The date is within the latest held compilation's known span, but the Register's record at capture does not confirm it was complete and in force."@en-AU .

tmk:VersionDateUnknown a tmk:VersionState ; rdfs:label "no date"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "The date that decides which text applies is not given. An explicit unknown: the held text is never assumed by default."@en-AU .

tmk:applicableDuring a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:range time:Interval ;
    rdfs:label "applicable during"@en-AU ;
    rdfs:comment "When a scoped statement holds, where it is narrower than the text it was read from: a transitional rule, a definition for one period. Defined for the model (A03) and not yet used: every record today was read against the held compilation, which its evidence hashes say."@en-AU .
